I/O Benchmark
=============
Test file size: 100 MB

========================================
Benchmark: I/O Methods Comparison
========================================

File size: 100 MB
Buffer size: 64 KB (for fwrite/write)

=== fwrite() with buffer=65536 bytes ===
Written: 104857600 bytes (requested 104857600)
Time: 0.085 seconds
Throughput: 1178.25 MB/s

=== write() with buffer=65536 bytes ===
Written: 104857600 bytes (requested 104857600)
Time: 0.066 seconds
Throughput: 1515.93 MB/s

=== write() with O_SYNC (buffer=65536 bytes) ===
Written: 104857600 bytes (requested 104857600)
Time: 4.100 seconds
Throughput: 24.39 MB/s

=== mmap() ===
Touched+msync: 104857600 bytes
Time: 0.981 seconds
Throughput: 101.95 MB/s

=== Summary ===
Fastest method: (compare results above)

Factors affecting performance:
- stdio (fwrite) has user-space buffering
- write() goes directly to kernel, but still uses page cache
- mmap() allows direct memory access, lazy writes (msync forces write)
- Actual disk speed depends on: HDD vs SSD, filesystem, etc.


